# ---------- Calibration private data (defence-in-depth) ----------
# Real captures, gold labels, relabel worksheets, order mappings and
# scoring reports live OUTSIDE every worktree; the calibration tools
# refuse in-repo paths (evals/extraction/tools/path_policy.py). These
# patterns are a narrow backstop for a hand-created file or a stray
# copy — they reduce the blast radius, they do NOT make an accidental
# commit impossible (a renamed or relocated file still slips past).
# Deliberately narrow: public fixtures (dataset.sample.jsonl,
# calibration/synthetic.jsonl, calibration/reference.jsonl) stay
# committable.
evals/extraction/dataset.v0.jsonl
evals/extraction/dataset.heldout.jsonl
evals/extraction/results/
evals/extraction/**/relabel/
evals/extraction/**/pseudonyms.json
evals/extraction/**/ambiguity-log.md

# ---------- Claude Code session state ----------
# Session state stays ignored, but versioned procedure skills are repo files
# (ADR-001: skills are executable governance, tested like code).
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
